<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="V850:LE:32:default">
<!--
    GH-7190: V850 BranchLessThan (SXB; CMP; BLT) decompiles to overflow-flag garbage.
    https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/issues/7190
    (GayHydra #477; kuna tests/stages/gh7190-ovlesssimplify.xml)

    Source loop:   do { ... } while (cVar5 < 8);   (signed byte counter compare)
    The V850 SLEIGH set_OV_neg macro models the OV flag through a sub-register
    sign shift instead of INT_SCARRY, so the BLT condition S != OV lifts to
        INT_SLESS(V+K, 0) != (signtest(V) && INT_SLESS(-1, V+K))
    with V+K computed twice.  RuleScarry never sees an INT_SCARRY, so the whole
    boolean leaks into the C.

    kuna ships RuleOvLessSimplify default-on and toggles it off for its second
    pass; the fork registers the rule behind "option ovlesssimplify" (default
    off = stock output) and swaps the passes.  Variable names are the fork's
    (iVar6, cVar5), and the fork prints the stock OV limb as "-1 < x - 8"
    where kuna's canonical compare form prints "0 <= x + -8".  The test can
    only run once the cspec spells CTBP correctly (GayHydra #509).

    Pass 1 (default): assertion #1 proves the bug reproduces.
    Pass 2 (option ovlesssimplify on): assertion #2 proves the rule collapses
    the condition to a clean signed byte compare against 8.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x0">
06f0e7008056a5a5b51560085f3a007241f2ca660100a152c16e01002c69b205aa56f76b4172a10aae006872b6f5e039dfed7f00
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x0" name="FUN_00000000"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>map fun r0x0 FUN_00000000</com>
  <com>lo fu FUN_00000000</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option ovlesssimplify on</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="GH7190 #1: default output keeps the OV-flag garbage condition (bug reproduced)" min="1" max="1">while \(\w+ - 8 &lt; 0 != \(\w+ &gt;&gt; 7 &lt; '\\0' &amp;&amp; -1 &lt; \w+ - 8\)\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GH7190 #2: ovlesssimplify on collapses the condition to a clean signed byte compare" min="1" max="1">while \(\w+ &lt; '\\b'\);</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
